Post-Exploitation Activities
After obtaining root privileges, the attacker gained unrestricted control over the target system. With root-level access, it is possible to perform several administrative operations that are normally restricted to privileged users.
These actions may include:
Accessing and modifying sensitive system files.
Viewing protected directories such as /root and system configuration files.
Creating or modifying user accounts.
Installing or executing additional tools or scripts.
Maintaining persistence on the system.
This level of access demonstrates that the attacker can fully control the machine and potentially compromise the confidentiality, integrity, and availability of the system.
